  "publishedAt": "2026-04-17T03:55:54.000Z",
  "content": "<div id=\"readability-page-1\" class=\"page\"><div> <p>From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</p> </div><div lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\" id=\"mw-content-text\">\n\n<table><tbody><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Highly accelerated region 1A/1B</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:HAR1F_RF00635_rna_secondary_structure.jpg\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/HAR1F_RF00635_rna_secondary_structure.jpg/250px-HAR1F_RF00635_rna_secondary_structure.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"342\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/HAR1F_RF00635_rna_secondary_structure.jpg/500px-HAR1F_RF00635_rna_secondary_structure.jpg 2x\" data-file-width=\"672\" data-file-height=\"918\"></a></span><div><p>Predicted <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secondary_structure\" title=\"Secondary structure\">secondary structure</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sequence_conservation\" title=\"Sequence conservation\">sequence conservation</a> of HAR1A</p></div></td></tr><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Identifiers</th></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Symbol</th><td>HAR1A</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rfam\" title=\"Rfam\">Rfam</a></th><td><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://rfam.org/family/RF00635\">RF00635</a></td></tr><tr><th colspan=\"2\">Other data</th></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RNA\" title=\"RNA\">RNA</a> type</th><td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gene\" title=\"Gene\">Gene</a>; <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_non-coding_RNA\" title=\"Long non-coding RNA\">lncRNA</a></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domain_(biology)\" title=\"Domain (biology)\">Domain</a></th><td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eukaryota\" title=\"Eukaryota\">Eukaryota</a>;</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sequence_Ontology\" title=\"Sequence Ontology\">SO</a></th><td><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.sequenceontology.org/miso/current_release/term/SO:0001463\">SO:0001463</a></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protein_Data_Bank\" title=\"Protein Data Bank\">PDB</a> structures</th><td><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/pdbe/entry/search/index/?searchParams=%7B%22rfam_accession%22:%5B%7B%22value%22:%22RF00635%22,%22condition1%22:%22AND%22,%22condition2%22:%22Equal%20to%22%7D%5D,%22resultState%22:%7B%22tabIndex%22:0,%22paginationIndex%22:1,%22perPage%22:%2210%22,%22sortBy%22:%22release_date%20desc%22%7D%7D\">PDBe</a></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>In molecular biology, <b>Human Accelerated Region 1</b> (Highly Accelerated Region 1, HAR1) is a segment of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_genome\" title=\"Human genome\">human genome</a> found on the long arm of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chromosome_20\" title=\"Chromosome 20\">chromosome 20</a>. It is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_accelerated_region\" title=\"Human accelerated region\">human accelerated region</a>. It is located within a pair of overlapping <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_non-coding_RNA\" title=\"Long non-coding RNA\">long non-coding RNA</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genes\" title=\"Genes\">genes</a>, HAR1A (HAR1F) and HAR1B (HAR1R).<sup id=\"cite_ref-Pollard2006_1-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Pollard2006-1\"><span>[</span>1<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<meta property=\"mw:PageProp/toc\">\n\n<p>HAR1A is expressed in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cajal%E2%80%93Retzius_cell\" title=\"Cajal–Retzius cell\">Cajal–Retzius cells</a>, contemporaneously with the protein <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reelin\" title=\"Reelin\">reelin</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Pollard2006_1-1\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Pollard2006-1\"><span>[</span>1<span>]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-pmid17040131_2-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-pmid17040131-2\"><span>[</span>2<span>]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-pmid16990130_3-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-pmid16990130-3\"><span>[</span>3<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>HAR1A was identified in August 2006 when human accelerated regions (HARs) were first investigated. These 49 regions represent parts of the human genome that differ significantly from highly conserved regions of our closest ancestors in terms of evolution. Many of the HARs are associated with genes known to play a role in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neural_development\" title=\"Neural development\">neurodevelopment</a>. One particularly altered region, HAR1, was found in a stretch of genome with no known protein-coding RNA sequences. Two RNA genes, HAR1F and HAR1R, were identified partly within the region. The RNA structure of HAR1A has been shown to be stable, with a secondary structure unlike those previously described.\n</p><p>HAR1A is active in the developing human brain between the 7th and 18th gestational weeks. It is found in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorsum_(biology)\" title=\"Dorsum (biology)\">dorsal</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telencephalon\" title=\"Telencephalon\">telencephalon</a> in fetuses. In adult humans, it is found throughout the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cerebellum\" title=\"Cerebellum\">cerebellum</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forebrain\" title=\"Forebrain\">forebrain</a>; it is also found in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Testes\" title=\"Testes\">testes</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Pollard2006_1-2\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Pollard2006-1\"><span>[</span>1<span>]</span></a></sup> There is evidence that HAR1 is repressed by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RE1-silencing_transcription_factor\" title=\"RE1-silencing transcription factor\">REST</a> in individuals with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huntington%27s_disease\" title=\"Huntington's disease\">Huntington's disease</a>, perhaps contributing to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neurodegeneration\" title=\"Neurodegeneration\">neurodegeneration</a> associated with the disease.<sup id=\"cite_ref-pmid20179156_4-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-pmid20179156-4\"><span>[</span>4<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Further work on the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RNA_structure\" title=\"RNA structure\">secondary structure</a> of HAR1A has suggested that the human form adopts a different fold to that of other mammals exemplified by the chimpanzee sequence.<sup id=\"cite_ref-pmid18511501_5-0\"><a href=\"#cite_note-pmid18511501-5\"><span>[</span>5<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n\n<p>The HAR1B gene overlaps HAR1A, and is located on the opposite <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DNA_strand\" title=\"DNA strand\">strand</a> of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chromosome\" title=\"Chromosome\">chromosome</a>. Its expression in the human brain is lower than that of HAR1A.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Pollard2006_1-3\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Pollard2006-1\"><span>[</span>1<span>]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-coding_RNA\" title=\"Non-coding RNA\">Non-coding RNA</a></li></ul>\n\n<div><ol>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Pollard2006-1\"><span>^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Pollard2006_1-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Pollard2006_1-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Pollard2006_1-2\"><sup><i><b>c</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Pollard2006_1-3\"><sup><i><b>d</b></i></sup></a></span> <span><cite id=\"CITEREFPollardSalamaLambertLambot2006\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katherine_Pollard\" title=\"Katherine Pollard\">Pollard KS</a>, Salama SR, Lambert N, Lambot MA, Coppens S, Pedersen JS, Katzman S, King B, Onodera C, Siepel A, Kern AD, Dehay C, Igel H, Ares M Jr, Vanderhaeghen P, Haussler D (2006-08-16). <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://dipot.ulb.ac.be/dspace/bitstream/2013/51805/3/pollard2006.pdf\">\"An RNA gene expressed during cortical development evolved rapidly in humans\"</a> <span>(PDF)</span>. <i>Nature</i>. <b>443</b> (7108): <span>167–</span>172. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bibcode_(identifier)\" title=\"Bibcode (identifier)\">Bibcode</a>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2006Natur.443..167P\">2006Natur.443..167P</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)\" title=\"Doi (identifier)\">doi</a>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038%2Fnature05113\">10.1038/nature05113</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hdl_(identifier)\" title=\"Hdl (identifier)\">hdl</a>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://hdl.handle.net/2013%2FULB-DIPOT%3Aoai%3Adipot.ulb.ac.be%3A2013%2F51805\">2013/ULB-DIPOT:oai:dipot.ulb.ac.be:2013/51805</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMID_(identifier)\" title=\"PMID (identifier)\">PMID</a>&nbsp;<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16915236\">16915236</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)\" title=\"S2CID (identifier)\">S2CID</a>&nbsp;<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:18107797\">18107797</a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Nature&amp;rft.atitle=An+RNA+gene+expressed+during+cortical+development+evolved+rapidly+in+humans&amp;rft.volume=443&amp;rft.issue=7108&amp;rft.pages=167-172&amp;rft.date=2006-08-16&amp;rft_id=info%3Ahdl%2F2013%2FULB-DIPOT%3Aoai%3Adipot.ulb.ac.be%3A2013%2F51805&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A18107797%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft_id=info%3Abibcode%2F2006Natur.443..167P&amp;rft_id=info%3Apmid%2F16915236&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1038%2Fnature05113&amp;rft.aulast=Pollard&amp;rft.aufirst=KS&amp;rft.au=Salama%2C+SR&amp;rft.au=Lambert%2C+N&amp;rft.au=Lambot%2C+MA&amp;rft.au=Coppens%2C+S&amp;rft.au=Pedersen%2C+JS&amp;rft.au=Katzman%2C+S&amp;rft.au=King%2C+B&amp;rft.au=Onodera%2C+C&amp;rft.au=Siepel%2C+A&amp;rft.au=Kern%2C+AD&amp;rft.au=Dehay%2C+C&amp;rft.au=Igel%2C+H&amp;rft.au=Ares+M+Jr&amp;rft.au=Vanderhaeghen%2C+P&amp;rft.au=Haussler%2C+D&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdipot.ulb.ac.be%2Fdspace%2Fbitstream%2F2013%2F51805%2F3%2Fpollard2006.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHuman+accelerated+region+1\"></span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.nature.com/nature/journal/v443/n7108/extref/nature05113-s1.doc\">supplement</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-pmid17040131-2\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-pmid17040131_2-0\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite id=\"CITEREFPollardSalamaKing2006\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katherine_Pollard\" title=\"Katherine Pollard\">Pollard KS</a>, Salama SR, King B, et&nbsp;al. (October 2006). <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1599772\">\"Forces shaping the fastest evolving regions in the human genome\"</a>. <i>PLOS Genet</i>. <b>2</b> (10): e168. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)\" title=\"Doi (identifier)\">doi</a>:<span title=\"Freely accessible\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1371%2Fjournal.pgen.0020168\">10.1371/journal.pgen.0020168</a></span>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMC_(identifier)\" title=\"PMC (identifier)\">PMC</a>&nbsp;<span title=\"Freely accessible\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1599772\">1599772</a></span>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMID_(identifier)\" title=\"PMID (identifier)\">PMID</a>&nbsp;<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17040131\">17040131</a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=PLOS+Genet.&amp;rft.atitle=Forces+shaping+the+fastest+evolving+regions+in+the+human+genome&amp;rft.volume=2&amp;rft.issue=10&amp;rft.pages=e168&amp;rft.date=2006-10&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov%2Fpmc%2Farticles%2FPMC1599772%23id-name%3DPMC&amp;rft_id=info%3Apmid%2F17040131&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1371%2Fjournal.pgen.0020168&amp;rft.aulast=Pollard&amp;rft.aufirst=KS&amp;rft.au=Salama%2C+SR&amp;rft.au=King%2C+B&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov%2Fpmc%2Farticles%2FPMC1599772&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHuman+accelerated+region+1\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-pmid16990130-3\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-pmid16990130_3-0\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite id=\"CITEREFAmadioWalsh2006\">Amadio JP, Walsh CA (September 2006). <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016%2Fj.cell.2006.09.007\">\"Brain evolution and uniqueness in the human genome\"</a>. <i>Cell</i>. <b>126</b> (6): <span>1033–</span>1035. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)\" title=\"Doi (identifier)\">doi</a>:<span title=\"Freely accessible\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016%2Fj.cell.2006.09.007\">10.1016/j.cell.2006.09.007</a></span>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMID_(identifier)\" title=\"PMID (identifier)\">PMID</a>&nbsp;<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16990130\">16990130</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)\" title=\"S2CID (identifier)\">S2CID</a>&nbsp;<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:16034905\">16034905</a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Cell&amp;rft.atitle=Brain+evolution+and+uniqueness+in+the+human+genome&amp;rft.volume=126&amp;rft.issue=6&amp;rft.pages=1033-1035&amp;rft.date=2006-09&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A16034905%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft_id=info%3Apmid%2F16990130&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1016%2Fj.cell.2006.09.007&amp;rft.aulast=Amadio&amp;rft.aufirst=JP&amp;rft.au=Walsh%2C+CA&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdoi.org%2F10.1016%252Fj.cell.2006.09.007&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHuman+accelerated+region+1\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-pmid20179156-4\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-pmid20179156_4-0\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite id=\"CITEREFJohnsonRichterJauchGaughwin2010\">Johnson R, Richter N, Jauch R, Gaughwin PM, Zuccato C, Cattaneo E, Stanton LW (2010). \"The Human Accelerated Region 1 noncoding RNA is repressed by REST in Huntington's disease\". <i>Physiol Genomics</i>. <b>41</b> (3): <span>269–</span>274. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)\" title=\"Doi (identifier)\">doi</a>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1152%2Fphysiolgenomics.00019.2010\">10.1152/physiolgenomics.00019.2010</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMID_(identifier)\" title=\"PMID (identifier)\">PMID</a>&nbsp;<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20179156\">20179156</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S2CID_(identifier)\" title=\"S2CID (identifier)\">S2CID</a>&nbsp;<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusID:25653037\">25653037</a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Physiol+Genomics&amp;rft.atitle=The+Human+Accelerated+Region+1+noncoding+RNA+is+repressed+by+REST+in+Huntington%27s+disease.&amp;rft.volume=41&amp;rft.issue=3&amp;rft.pages=269-274&amp;rft.date=2010&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapi.semanticscholar.org%2FCorpusID%3A25653037%23id-name%3DS2CID&amp;rft_id=info%3Apmid%2F20179156&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1152%2Fphysiolgenomics.00019.2010&amp;rft.aulast=Johnson&amp;rft.aufirst=R&amp;rft.au=Richter%2C+N&amp;rft.au=Jauch%2C+R&amp;rft.au=Gaughwin%2C+PM&amp;rft.au=Zuccato%2C+C&amp;rft.au=Cattaneo%2C+E&amp;rft.au=Stanton%2C+LW&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHuman+accelerated+region+1\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-pmid18511501-5\"><span><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-pmid18511501_5-0\">^</a></b></span> <span><cite id=\"CITEREFBeniaminovWesthofKrol2008\">Beniaminov A, Westhof E, Krol A (July 2008). <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2441984\">\"Distinctive structures between chimpanzee and human in a brain noncoding RNA\"</a>. <i>RNA</i>. <b>14</b> (7): <span>1270–</span>1275. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)\" title=\"Doi (identifier)\">doi</a>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1261%2Frna.1054608\">10.1261/rna.1054608</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMC_(identifier)\" title=\"PMC (identifier)\">PMC</a>&nbsp;<span title=\"Freely accessible\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2441984\">2441984</a></span>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMID_(identifier)\" title=\"PMID (identifier)\">PMID</a>&nbsp;<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18511501\">18511501</a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=RNA&amp;rft.atitle=Distinctive+structures+between+chimpanzee+and+human+in+a+brain+noncoding+RNA&amp;rft.volume=14&amp;rft.issue=7&amp;rft.pages=1270-1275&amp;rft.date=2008-07&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov%2Fpmc%2Farticles%2FPMC2441984%23id-name%3DPMC&amp;rft_id=info%3Apmid%2F18511501&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1261%2Frna.1054608&amp;rft.aulast=Beniaminov&amp;rft.aufirst=A&amp;rft.au=Westhof%2C+E&amp;rft.au=Krol%2C+A&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov%2Fpmc%2Farticles%2FPMC2441984&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AHuman+accelerated+region+1\"></span></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20071014180845/http://www.sciam.com/article.cfm?chanID=sa003&amp;articleID=00023D61-9116-14E3-911683414B7F0000\">Scientists Identify Gene Difference Between Humans and Chimps</a>, <i>Scientific American</i>, 17 August 2006</li></ul>\n\n<ul><li></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://rfam.xfam.org/family?entry=RF00635\">Page for Human accelerated region 1F</a> at <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rfam\" title=\"Rfam\">Rfam</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgTracks?org=human&amp;db=hg17&amp;hgt.out3=1.5x&amp;position=chr20%3A61203966-61204071\">UCSC genome browser page for Human accelerated region 1F</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐web.eqiad.main‐6897878f94‐ckcgn\nCached time: 20260403131824\nCache expiry: 2592000\nCache expiry source: Module:Citation/CS1 (os.date(%Y))\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.253 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.409 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 981/1000000\nRevision size: 5350/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 24743/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 1567/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 12/100\nExpensive parser function count: 1/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 1/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 25288/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.143/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 4802396/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 0/500\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  273.960 1 -total\n 45.57%  124.850 1 Template:Reflist\n 37.04%  101.484 5 Template:Cite_journal\n 27.92% 76.495 2 Template:Short_description\n 26.23% 71.850 1 Template:Infobox_rfam\n 21.59% 59.146 1 Template:Infobox\n 15.85% 43.423 4 Template:Pagetype 9.20% 25.211 8 Template:Main_other 5.61% 15.361 2 Template:SDcat 3.56% 9.756 1 Template:Pluralize_from_text\n-->\n\n<!-- Render ID 97c719f7-2f5f-11f1-bd68-513b4572807c -->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key enwiki:pcache:6514087:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20260403131824 and revision id 1317480837. Rendering was triggered because: page_view\n -->\n</div></div>",
